WEBVTT

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:15.360
Kasuga-kun, you're slowing down.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.700
I'm getting a little tired.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:24.580
Hey,

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.560
what do you think is on the other side?

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:28.790
Huh?

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.790
I've always thought...

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.590
maybe there's nothing on the other side.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:43.650
Maybe that's where the world ends, 
and everything beyond

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:47.020
is just an inky black mess that 
goes on forever and ever...

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.860
So murky, you could die in it.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.360
I think I understand what you mean.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:01.120
There's nothing in this town...

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:05.200
Nothing, nowhere, no one...

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:11.630
Just rusted metal, pachinko parlors, and weeds.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.950
If I stay here, there's no hope for me.

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:17.370
I must escape...

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.280
Escape somewhere far away.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.520
I've always wanted to go on a journey.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.160
Huh? Journey?

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:26.440
What are you talking about?

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:28.940
I'm not interested in that, you scrap of shit!

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:29.680
Huh?

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:33.860
You just keep pedaling.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:35.970
On and on,

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:37.410
forever...

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:05.220
Nanako, you aren't hungry?

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:06.470
Hmm?

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.560
Not really.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:13.480
Oh, right!

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.260
Sorry to interrupt dinner,

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.570
but may I make a phone call?

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.940
Y-Yeah...

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:39.840
Hello, Nakamura residence.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.510
Ah, hello.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.180
I'm in Sawa-san's class.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.240
My name is Saeki.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:51.910
Um, is Sawa-san home?

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:53.600
Oh, I'm sorry...

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.400
She isn't home yet.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.900
Where could she have wandered off to...

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:00.840
Saeki-san, was it?

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:03.610
Are you a friend of Sawa's?

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.750
So she was able to make a friend.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:07.910
Um, sorry to bother you!

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.410
I understand! Thank you!

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:10.840
Eh, okay...

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:18.930
What's wrong? Are you okay?

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.840
I need to go to the stationery store.

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:26.260
I ran out of notebooks.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:28.970
I'll be right back.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:33.980
<b>Flowers of Evil</b>

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:33.980
<b>Episode 10 of 13</b>

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:40.360
We're barely moving, Kasuga-kun.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:42.780
Because...!

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:45.440
Pathetic...

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.100
You really are useless scrap.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.170
Hey!

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.130
I've been doing all the pedaling!

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.560
It's starting to rain...

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:01.210
Over there...

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:03.090
Let's take cover over there!

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:22.070
The town looks so small from here.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:31.290
I wonder if Dad has found out by now.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:36.040
<i>Help me to understand what's 
going through your mind!</i>

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:37.880
<i>I'll be waiting...</i>

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.170
<i>I'll be waiting!</i>

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:52.110
Got any money on you, Kasuga-kun?

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:55.200
No.

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:59.450
You're so worthless.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:02.520
But it isn't my fault...

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:03.970
I made a break for it!

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:08.570
What?

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.330
It's nothing.

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:16.960
I'm already bored.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:17.980
Let's go back.

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:18.830
Huh?

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:19.820
No way!

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.970
Just kidding.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:29.510
I'm itching to see what's on the other side.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:32.430
Once the rain stops, let's get going.

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:41.980
Nope, no idea.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:45.240
Why are you out so late?

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:54.440
Um, excuse me!

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:56.570
Sorry, we're closed for the day.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:00.190
Have you seen a middle school boy around?

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:00.830
Huh?

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:04.340
I mean...

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:08.760
Have you seen a boy and girl?

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:12.040
Yeah, they passed by an hour ago, on a bike.

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:15.140
No one ever goes through here on 
a bicycle, so I remember them.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.520
Really?

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:17.380
Which way?

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:18.480
Which way did they go?!

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:25.050
That way, but that road 
leads over the mountain.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:34.870
I wonder why.

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:36.250
Hmm?

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.780
Among those lights are other people

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:44.090
who will live their lives as usual tomorrow.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:52.080
So why are we out here?

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:57.360
That's obvious.

00:06:58.170 --> 00:06:59.600
Because we're sickos.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:05.920
Oh...

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:13.000
Then I guess I don't mind being a sicko.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:18.870
For some reason, I feel really good right now.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:27.960
Kasuga-kun...

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:30.050
It's not fair...

00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:31.800
Running away...

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.050
It's not fair!

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.100
Thank you, Nakamura-san...

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:40.230
For bringing me out here.

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:55.120
The rain isn't letting up.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.300
Oh, well.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.710
Let's get some sleep.

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:13.510
Come on, Kasuga-kun...

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:15.510
We have a long way to go.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:19.740
Yeah.

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:41.640
It's like that's

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:46.170
the sound of those shit-faces 
in town drowning in the sea.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:49.550
Nakamura-san...

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:07.740
Saeki-san...

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:34.620
Kasuga-kun,

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:37.790
I'm sorry.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:41.720
I pushed too hard, didn't I?

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:45.830
I'm sorry...

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:48.190
I'm sorry.

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:52.620
Saeki-san...

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.160
Why?

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:57.150
Why?

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:00.500
This book...

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:05.510
I'm sorry it got wet.

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:12.110
I've read it so many times.

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:17.880
But it's still too hard for me to understand.

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:23.890
I don't understand why you like this book...

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:26.490
Tell me...

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:31.080
What do you like about this book?

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:33.240
What's going on...

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:42.190
What's going on in your heart?

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:47.380
Please tell me...

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:49.950
Don't run away.

00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:54.730
We're supposed to be going out.

00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:59.010
So why do you turn to Nakamura-san?

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:01.260
The other side.

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:07.770
I'm going to the other side.

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.940
Kasuga-kun's tagging along.

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:11.630
The other side?

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:14.690
What other side?

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:20.360
Kasuga-kun...

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:25.170
It isn't...

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.750
It isn't like that.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:29.560
I...

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.280
I...

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:42.550
Are you in love with Nakamura-san?

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:44.850
Eh?

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:49.480
I-I'm not!

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:58.360
Do you really want to know what's 
going on inside Kasuga-kun?

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:02.150
Then I'll tell you.

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:05.380
Nakamura-san?

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:10.200
Ever since he stole your gym uniform,

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:13.040
I've been watching him.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:16.600
Know what he was wearing under his 
clothes when he asked you o—

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:17.670
Nakamura-san...

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:22.050
Take them off!

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:22.970
Take off your clothes!

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:23.530
Stop it!

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:27.720
When Kasuga-kun went on that stupid date 
with you and asked you to go steady,

00:12:28.070 --> 00:12:31.530
he was rock-hard, wearing that 
damn gym uniform of yours

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:34.560
that he had sniffed and rubbed all over himself!

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.610
See it? Look...

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:46.470
All this time, Kasuga-kun's worn 
your uniform in his heart.

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:51.200
It's on his real self, under all 
those layers he hides beneath.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:55.500
Look at him all exposed...

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:59.000
This is why he's a real pervert.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:18.770
No matter what he's done...

00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:23.320
If Kasuga-kun did it because 
he cared about me,

00:13:24.180 --> 00:13:25.750
it makes me happy.

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:29.660
I don't think he's a pervert.

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:34.660
But...

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.610
Tell me these things!

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:40.390
I would accept you!

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:44.840
If there are things only she knows about you,

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:47.680
tell me everything!

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:59.100
Let's go back together...

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:06.600
Saeki-san,

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:08.510
I'm sorry.

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:10.680
I'm sorry...

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:37.510
Forget it, Kasuga-kun.

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:39.350
This is no fun.

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:41.270
Nakamura-san...

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:50.160
Spend the rest of your life rotting in 
this town like the shit-face you are.

00:14:56.900 --> 00:14:58.000
Kasuga-kun?

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:10.030
N-Nakamura-san!

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:14.850
Kasuga-kun!

00:15:17.990 --> 00:15:19.640
Kasuga-kun!

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:25.900
What?

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:30.650
Nakamura-san...

00:15:39.390 --> 00:15:40.900
Why?

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:44.330
Why are you chasing after Nakamura-san?

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:45.940
Why?!

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:57.310
Am I...

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:03.320
Am I not good enough?

00:16:04.820 --> 00:16:10.430
You really do care more 
about Nakamura-san...

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:13.630
N-No...

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:17.160
My body just moved on its own.

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:21.140
It isn't what you think...

00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:26.100
Stupid.

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:28.920
This is so stupid.

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:33.250
What's...

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:35.320
What's so stupid?

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:37.510
You have...

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:43.280
You have no idea what I've been 
going through, Nakamura-san!

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:48.110
Don't laugh...

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.100
Don't laugh at me!

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:55.910
I was really happy...

00:16:58.260 --> 00:17:00.040
Kasuga-kun

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:06.250
transformed me from a pebble into a jewel.

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:11.170
Saeki-san...

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:12.440
But now...

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:15.450
But now...

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:19.190
Why...

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:23.320
Why am I...

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:03.260
Kasuga-kun...

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:07.110
Kasuga-kun!

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:15.690
Make up your mind.

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:18.230
Are you coming?

00:18:18.230 --> 00:18:19.700
Or are you going back?

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:25.450
Stop tearing my soul apart.

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:42.120
I am...

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:47.920
I am an empty person.

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:55.910
I read <i>Flowers of Evil</i>.

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:58.780
Shibusawa Tatsuhiko,

00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:00.940
Breton,

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:03.120
Hagiwara Sakutarou,

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:04.830
and Bataille...

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.150
I read them all.

00:19:07.420 --> 00:19:10.830
But what does it matter?

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:14.620
I thought I was different.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:18.350
I thought I was different 
from all those other losers.

00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:21.760
But was I?

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:28.380
I don't actually understand 
Baudelaire or <i>Flowers of Evil</i>.

00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:33.480
I was just impressed with 
myself for reading it...

00:19:36.490 --> 00:19:38.430
I was trying not to see

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:41.220
who I really was.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:44.570
Didn't want to think I wasn't special.

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:48.380
I am

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:51.500
an empty person.

00:19:56.740 --> 00:19:58.400
Saeki-san...

00:20:00.580 --> 00:20:04.030
I've had a crush on you for such a long time.

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:08.850
I thought of you as my muse, my angel.

00:20:10.790 --> 00:20:13.380
I wanted you to stay an angel...

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:18.060
I didn't want to know your human side.

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:20.340
I'm scared!

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:24.800
I can't be normal...

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:28.180
I can't have a normal relationship!

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:35.050
But I'm not worthy of being called a pervert!

00:20:37.230 --> 00:20:42.060
I can't be the person Nakamura-san 
wants me to be, either...

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:46.270
I can't expose myself.

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:51.160
There's nothing for me to expose...

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:54.900
I'm a shit-face!

00:20:56.270 --> 00:21:01.080
I'm the biggest shit-face in the world!

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:04.980
I can't choose...

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:08.090
I can't do it!

00:21:09.190 --> 00:21:12.540
I don't have the right to choose!

00:21:29.440 --> 00:21:30.700
Fine.

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:33.390
I've had enough.

00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:20.770
Are you Saeki Nanako-san?

00:22:21.450 --> 00:22:24.000
Your parents requested a search for you.

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:25.110
We found her.

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:27.740
Yes, she's fine.

00:22:28.580 --> 00:22:30.620
All three of you, get in the car.

00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:33.080
You can tell us everything at the station.

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:34.870
Hey, wait!

00:22:35.670 --> 00:22:36.890
Stop!

00:22:38.900 --> 00:22:40.440
Stop!

00:22:41.180 --> 00:22:42.410
Hey!

00:22:45.640 --> 00:22:46.820
Let me go!

00:22:46.820 --> 00:22:48.760
Let me go, shit-face!

00:23:21.610 --> 00:23:24.070
There's nowhere for me to go.

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:24.960
Don't just stand there! Say something!

00:23:24.420 --> 00:23:26.530
Shut your damned mouth.

00:23:27.550 --> 00:23:28.990
Thank you for everything.

00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:29.780
Liar.

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:31.150
Let's break up.

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:34.180
I trusted you...

00:23:32.170 --> 00:23:33.450
Nakamura-san!

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:36.060
Nakamura-san!

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:40.980
<b>Why don't I rotoscope you, too?! 
